=begin
  vault-to-eddy.lic

  Moves what's in your vault at your hometown's Carousel into your Eddy, the
  effervescent eddy you wear: a portable vault that holds up to 250 things
  weighing up to 1700 stones, reached from anywhere through its watery
  portal. Everything goes except the vault's own large shelf. Then it closes
  the vault and leaves you in the Carousel.

  What ;stash wrote down is marked as in the Eddy, so ;unstash gets it back
  from there without walking to the Carousel, and ;stash puts things in the
  Eddy from then on. Weapons go too. A weapon or piece of gear from your
  yaml's gear list that ;stash didn't write down goes on the list as one of
  your weapons, so ;unstash weapons (which t2's hunt block runs first) puts
  it back where combat-trainer keeps it.

  It takes things out the way trash-sort does, by noun: "get deed from
  vault", into the Eddy, "get deed from vault" again, until the vault has no
  more deeds. Something that stays (the shelf, or what the Eddy won't take)
  is put back, and "get second deed" reaches the next one.

  A stash list entry that nothing in the vault answered to isn't there any
  more, so it comes off the list, as ;unstash would do. If the Eddy fills up,
  the rest stays in the vault and on the list, and nothing comes off it.

  Run it with empty hands, and not while t2, a crafting script, stash,
  unstash or trash-sort is running.

  Usage:
    ;vault-to-eddy
=end

# What ;stash put away. Shared with stash, unstash and trash-sort.
STASH_LIST = File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, 'stash.yaml')

# Scripts that use the stash list or the vault, or carry things around
BUSY_SCRIPTS = %w[t2 stash unstash trash-sort start_marathon taskmaster workorders].freeze

# The Eddy, from Fizzlestiks's first look at it (2026-11-27): you PUT things
# in the eddy, and GET and LOOK through its portal ("LOOK IN PORTAL -or LOOK
# IN WATERY PORTAL"). Always "my": LOOK IN PORT at the Strand looked in the
# meeting portal there. GET finds nothing until you LOOK in the portal
# (DRCI's get_item_from_eddy_portal? says so too).
EDDY = 'my eddy'
EDDY_PORTAL = 'my portal'
EDDY_OPENED = [/^You open/, /already open/i].freeze
EDDY_LOOKED = [/^In the .*/, /nothing in there/i].freeze
EDDY_UNREACHABLE = [/^What were you referring to/, /^I could not find/, /^I don't know what you are referring to/,
                    /funnel downward/, /^You can't/, /interfer/i].freeze
# "There isn't any more room in the eddy for that." (dr-scripts' own tests).
# The weight limit's message isn't known yet, so those are guesses.
EDDY_FULL = [/isn't any more room/i, /too heavy/i, /\bweight\b/i, /too many/i, /\bfull\b/i].freeze
# Just this one won't go in ("fit within the eddy container's dimensions")
EDDY_REFUSED = [/^You can't/, /^You must/, /\bfit\b/i, /too (?:big|large|long|wide|tall)/i, /^That's/, /^What were you referring to/].freeze

# Getting in and out of the vault: the same steps and messages as ;stash
ARCHES = ['go blackwood arch', 'go ironwood arch', 'go rosewood arch'].freeze
ARCH_IN = /escorts you through/
RENT_DUE = /\brent\b/i
ARCH_RESTRICTED = /access to that arch is restricted/
ARCH_BUSY = /is using that booth|blocks|someone|using|Sorry/
LEVER_PULLED = /door pops open/
VAULT_OPENED = [/^The vault opens/, /already open/i].freeze
CHAMBER = /Chamber/
CAROUSEL_CHAMBER = /Carousel Chamber/
CAROUSEL_BOOTH = /Carousel Booth/

# bput returns only the matched text, so these run to the end of the line.
# RUMMAGE lists the whole vault: "You rummage through a secure vault and see
# a large shelf, some heavy wool cloth and a massive selatila shard."
RUMMAGED = /^You rummage .* and see .*/
RUMMAGED_EMPTY = /^You rummage .* but there is nothing in there/
VAULT_LIST = /^In the .* you see .*/
VAULT_EMPTY = /^There is nothing in there/
GET_SUCCESS = [/^You get .*/, /^You pick up .*/].freeze
NOT_FOUND = [/^What were you referring to/, /^I could not find/, /^I don't know what you are referring to/].freeze
GET_REFUSED = [/^You need a free hand/, /^You can't/, /^Please rephrase/].freeze
PUT_SUCCESS = [/^You put .*/].freeze

# The vault's own furniture, which stays: the large shelf ("container - vault
# storage", 2026-11-25)
VAULT_FURNITURE = /\b(?:shelf|shelves|rack|cabinet|bookcase|armoire)\z/i

# Lich's $ORDINALS: how far "get second deed", "get third deed" ... can count
ORDINALS = %w[first second third fourth fifth sixth seventh eighth ninth tenth eleventh twelfth thirteenth
              fourteenth fifteenth sixteenth seventeenth eighteenth nineteenth twentieth].freeze
# Words that follow the noun in a long name, as RUMMAGE gives them (trash-sort's)
AFTER_NOUN = /\A(?:for|of|with|from|in|on|at|marked|comprised|tipped|sharpened|engraved|carved|shaped|inlaid|
                wrapped|bearing|featuring|covered|crafted|made|set|trimmed|adorned|embroidered|slung|decorated|
                painted|etched|studded|bound|lined|edged|depicting|showing|filled|holding|containing|accented|
                hung|tied|strung)\z/xi
# "pair of scissors", "handful of time slips": the noun is the last word
MEASURES = /\A(?:pair|handful|bunch|bundle|piece|bit|scrap|set)\z/i

def hands_empty?
  DRC.right_hand.nil? && DRC.left_hand.nil?
end

# The hand display and room title can lag the game text by a moment
def settle
  10.times do
    return true if yield

    pause 0.1
  end
  false
end

def in_room?(pattern)
  [XMLData.room_title, XMLData.room_name].any? { |title| title.to_s =~ pattern }
end

def in_chamber?
  in_room?(CHAMBER)
end

# Opens the Eddy and LOOKs in its portal, which GET needs first. False if
# you don't have one or can't reach it here.
def eddy_ready?
  opened = DRC.bput("open #{EDDY}", *EDDY_OPENED, *EDDY_UNREACHABLE)
  return false unless EDDY_OPENED.any? { |pattern| opened =~ pattern }

  looked = DRC.bput("look in #{EDDY_PORTAL}", *EDDY_LOOKED, *EDDY_UNREACHABLE)
  EDDY_LOOKED.any? { |pattern| looked =~ pattern }
end

# Walks to the hometown's Carousel and opens your vault, starting from the
# chamber or a booth if you're in one already. Remembers how far it got in
# @vault_steps so leave_vault can undo it. Says why and returns false if it
# can't.
def open_vault(settings)
  @vault_steps = []
  if in_room?(CAROUSEL_CHAMBER)
    @vault_steps.push(:booth, :chamber)
  else
    return false unless into_booth(settings)
    return false unless into_chamber
  end

  result = DRC.bput('open vault', *VAULT_OPENED, RENT_DUE, *NOT_FOUND, /^You can't/)
  unless VAULT_OPENED.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern }
    DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: the vault didn't open: #{result.empty? ? 'no reply' : result}")
    return false
  end
  @vault_steps << :open
  true
end

# To the hometown's Carousel and through an arch, unless you're in a booth
# already
def into_booth(settings)
  if in_room?(CAROUSEL_BOOTH)
    @vault_steps << :booth
    return true
  end

  room = get_data('town')[settings.hometown]&.dig('vault', 'id')
  unless room
    DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: no vault listed for your hometown, #{settings.hometown}.")
    return false
  end
  unless DRCT.walk_to(room)
    DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: couldn't walk to the Carousel (room #{room}).")
    return false
  end
  enter_booth
end

# From the booth through its door into the vault chamber
def into_chamber
  unless DRC.bput('pull lever', LEVER_PULLED, *NOT_FOUND, /^You can't/) =~ LEVER_PULLED
    DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: pulling the lever didn't open the door.")
    return false
  end

  DRC.bput('go door', /.+/)
  unless settle { in_chamber? }
    DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: GO DOOR didn't reach the Carousel Chamber. Room: #{XMLData.room_title.inspect}")
    return false
  end
  @vault_steps << :chamber
  true
end

# Through the first arch whose booth is free, waiting a while if all are in use
def enter_booth
  6.times do
    ARCHES.each do |arch|
      result = DRC.bput(arch, ARCH_IN, RENT_DUE, ARCH_RESTRICTED, ARCH_BUSY, *NOT_FOUND)
      if result =~ ARCH_IN
        @vault_steps << :booth
        return true
      end
      if result =~ RENT_DUE
        DRC.message('vault-to-eddy: vault rent is due. Pay it at the Carousel desk (GO DESK), then try again.')
        return false
      end
      if NOT_FOUND.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern }
        DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: there's no #{arch.split[1]} arch here, so stopping.")
        return false
      end
    end
    DRC.message('vault-to-eddy: every booth is busy. Waiting 10 seconds.')
    pause 10
  end
  DRC.message('vault-to-eddy: gave up waiting for a free booth.')
  false
end

# Closes the vault and goes back out to the Carousel, as far as open_vault got
def leave_vault
  steps = @vault_steps.to_a
  DRC.bput('close vault', /^You close the vault/, /already closed/i, /isn't open/i, *NOT_FOUND) if steps.include?(:open)
  DRC.bput('go door', /.+/) if steps.include?(:chamber)
  DRC.bput('go arch', /door slams closed/, /.+/) if steps.include?(:booth)
  @vault_steps = []
end

# What's in the vault, by the names RUMMAGE gives (LOOK IN if RUMMAGE doesn't
# answer, which can stop short of a full vault), or nil if neither answers
def vault_contents
  result = DRC.bput('rummage vault', RUMMAGED, RUMMAGED_EMPTY, *NOT_FOUND)
  return [] if result =~ RUMMAGED_EMPTY

  if result =~ RUMMAGED
    listed = result.sub(/^You rummage .*? and see /, '')
  else
    result = DRC.bput('look in vault', VAULT_LIST, VAULT_EMPTY, *NOT_FOUND)
    return [] if result =~ VAULT_EMPTY
    return nil unless result =~ VAULT_LIST

    listed = result.sub(/^In the .*? you see /, '')
  end
  listed.sub(/\A(?:some|an|a) /, '').sub(/\.\z/, '')
        .split(/(?:,|\band) (?:some|an|a) /).map(&:strip).reject(&:empty?)
end

# The noun GET takes, which in a long name comes before one of AFTER_NOUN:
# "deed FOR a lelori log", "flask OF oil" (trash-sort's)
def noun_of(name)
  words = name.split
  at = (1...words.size).find { |index| words[index] =~ AFTER_NOUN }
  return words.last if at.nil? || (words[at - 1] =~ MEASURES && words[at].casecmp?('of'))

  words[at - 1]
end

# What GET handed over: "You get a concise contract marked with the crest of
# the Traders' Guild from inside a secure vault." gives the contract's name
def got_name(result)
  result[/^You (?:get|pick up) (?:an? |some |the |your )?(.+?) from inside\b/, 1] ||
    result[/^You (?:get|pick up) (?:an? |some |the |your )?(.+?)(?: (?:from|off) .*)?\.?\z/, 1]
end

# Every word of one of these names is in the name ("gilt dagger" in "gilt
# steel dagger")
def named?(name, names)
  words = name.to_s.downcase.split
  names.any? do |wanted|
    wanted_words = wanted.to_s.downcase.tr('.', ' ').split
    !wanted_words.empty? && (wanted_words - words).empty?
  end
end

# Your yaml's gear list (weapons, armor, shields), as the short names
# EquipmentManager uses: "basket-hilt.cutlass". Only ones with an adjective:
# a bare "gloves" would claim any gloves in the vault.
def gear_short_names(settings)
  settings.gear.to_a.filter_map do |piece|
    next unless piece.is_a?(Hash)

    adjective = piece[:adjective] || piece['adjective']
    name = piece[:name] || piece['name']
    "#{adjective}.#{name}" if adjective && name
  end
end

# What ;stash weapons wrote down: no name, just the short name
def weapon_entry?(entry)
  entry['from'] == 'gear' || entry['for'].to_a.include?('weapons')
end

# Why this stays in the vault, or nil if it goes to the Eddy
def stays_reason(name)
  return 'the vault\'s own' if noun_of(name) =~ VAULT_FURNITURE

  nil
end

# The stash list entry still marked as in the vault that this is, if any: the
# same name, or one whose every word is in it ("deed for a lelori log" in
# "deed for a thick lelori log"). A weapon's entry goes by its short name
# ("basket-hilt.cutlass" in "basket-hilt cutlass").
def entry_for(got)
  open = @stash_list.reject { |entry| entry['in'] == 'eddy' || @marked.any? { |done| done.equal?(entry) } }
  open.find { |entry| entry['name'].to_s.casecmp?(got) } ||
    open.select { |entry| entry['name'] && named?(got, [entry['name']]) }.max_by { |entry| entry['name'].length } ||
    open.find { |entry| entry['name'].nil? && weapon_entry?(entry) && named?(got, [entry['item']]) }
end

# A new entry for a piece of your gear that wasn't on the list, as ;stash
# weapons writes one, so ;unstash weapons gets it back before a hunt
def gear_entry_for(got)
  short = @gear.select { |each| named?(got, [each]) }.max_by(&:length)
  short && { 'item' => short, 'name' => nil, 'from' => 'gear', 'for' => ['weapons'], 'in' => 'eddy' }
end

def save_stash_list
  File.write(STASH_LIST, @stash_list.to_yaml)
end

# Back in the vault. Stops the script if it's still in your hand.
def back_in_vault(noun)
  return if DRC.bput("put my #{noun} in vault", *PUT_SUCCESS, *NOT_FOUND, /no room/i, /^You can't/) =~ PUT_SUCCESS.first && settle { hands_empty? }

  DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: couldn't put the #{noun} back in the vault. It's still in your hand, so stopping.")
  exit
end

# Puts what's in hand in the Eddy: :put, :full, or :refused. Empty hands
# after are what count, as its messages aren't all known yet.
def into_eddy(noun)
  result = DRC.bput("put my #{noun} in #{EDDY}", *PUT_SUCCESS, *EDDY_FULL, *EDDY_REFUSED)
  return :put if settle { hands_empty? }
  return :full if EDDY_FULL.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern }

  :refused
end

# Moves everything under this noun: "get deed from vault" again and again,
# each into the Eddy. Something that stays is put back, and the next ordinal
# reaches past it. Returns :done, :full, or :ordinals (more stayed than GET
# can count past).
def move_noun(noun)
  stayed = 0
  loop do
    return :ordinals if stayed >= ORDINALS.size

    asked = stayed.zero? ? noun : "#{ORDINALS[stayed]} #{noun}"
    result = DRC.bput("get #{asked} from vault", *GET_SUCCESS, *NOT_FOUND, *GET_REFUSED)
    return :done unless GET_SUCCESS.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern } && settle { !hands_empty? }

    got = got_name(result) || noun
    reason = stays_reason(got)
    if reason
      back_in_vault(noun)
      @stayed[reason] << got unless @stayed[reason].include?(got)
      stayed += 1
      next
    end

    case into_eddy(noun)
    when :put
      @refused_first = 0
      @moved << got
      entry = entry_for(got)
      if entry
        entry['in'] = 'eddy'
      else
        entry = gear_entry_for(got)
        next unless entry

        @stash_list << entry
        @added << got
      end
      @marked << entry
      save_stash_list
    when :full
      back_in_vault(noun)
      return :full
    else
      back_in_vault(noun)
      @stayed["the Eddy wouldn't take it"] << got
      stayed += 1
      # The first three all refused: the Eddy doesn't work in here
      @refused_first += 1 if @moved.empty?
      return :unreachable if @refused_first >= 3
    end
  end
end

running = BUSY_SCRIPTS.select { |name| Script.running?(name) }
unless running.empty?
  DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: #{running.join(', ')} #{running.size > 1 ? 'are' : 'is'} running. Run this once nothing else is.")
  exit
end
unless hands_empty?
  DRC.message('vault-to-eddy: empty your hands first.')
  exit
end
unless eddy_ready?
  DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: couldn't open your Eddy and look in its portal here. Are you wearing it?")
  exit
end

settings = get_settings
@stash_list = File.exist?(STASH_LIST) ? YAML.safe_load(File.read(STASH_LIST)) || [] : []
@gear = gear_short_names(settings)
@moved = []
@marked = []
@added = []
@stayed = Hash.new { |hash, reason| hash[reason] = [] }
@refused_first = 0
stopped = nil
left = nil

begin
  exit unless open_vault(settings)
  # The Eddy has to work in the vault chamber too
  unless eddy_ready?
    DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: couldn't reach your Eddy's portal from the vault chamber, so nothing's moved.")
    exit
  end

  names = vault_contents
  if names.nil?
    DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: RUMMAGE VAULT and LOOK IN VAULT didn't say what's in it, so nothing's moved.")
    exit
  end

  names.reject { |name| stays_reason(name) }.map { |name| noun_of(name).downcase }.uniq.each do |noun|
    outcome = move_noun(noun)
    next if outcome == :done

    stopped = outcome
    break if %i[full unreachable].include?(outcome)
  end
  left = vault_contents
ensure
  leave_vault
end

dropped = []
# Only when every noun was emptied: then a listed thing nothing answered to
# isn't in the vault (or is still there under a name it does answer to)
if stopped.nil? && left
  gone = @stash_list.reject do |entry|
    entry['in'] == 'eddy' || weapon_entry?(entry) || entry['name'].nil? || @marked.any? { |done| done.equal?(entry) } ||
      left.any? { |name| entry['name'] && named?(name, [entry['name']]) }
  end
  dropped = gone.map { |entry| entry['name'] || entry['item'] }
  unless gone.empty?
    @stash_list.reject! { |entry| gone.any? { |each| each.equal?(entry) } }
    save_stash_list
  end
end

tally = ->(names) { names.tally.map { |name, count| count > 1 ? "#{name} (#{count})" : name }.join(', ') }
if @moved.empty?
  DRC.message('vault-to-eddy: nothing moved into the Eddy.')
else
  DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: moved #{@moved.size} thing(s) into your Eddy: #{tally.call(@moved)}")
  listed = @marked.size - @added.size
  DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: #{listed} of them were on the stash list, now marked as in the Eddy. ;unstash gets them from there.") unless listed.zero?
  DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: your gear, put on the stash list so ;unstash weapons gets it back before a hunt: #{@added.join(', ')}") unless @added.empty?
end
@stayed.each { |reason, names| DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: left in the vault (#{reason}): #{names.join(', ')}") }
DRC.message('vault-to-eddy: the Eddy is full, so the rest is still in the vault and on the list.') if stopped == :full
DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: the Eddy wouldn't take the first three things, so stopping. Everything's still in the vault and on the list.") if stopped == :unreachable
DRC.message('vault-to-eddy: more of one noun stayed than GET can count past, so some may be left. Run it again to check.') if stopped == :ordinals
DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: on the stash list but not in the vault, dropped from the list: #{dropped.join(', ')}") unless dropped.empty?
DRC.message("vault-to-eddy: still in the vault: #{left.empty? ? 'nothing' : tally.call(left)}") if left
